20:07.624 --> 20:09.625
for, what, 20-something years?

20:09.626 --> 20:14.422
It's, like, if you
get it wrong, oh, my God.

20:14.547 --> 20:17.091
Thunder and lightning
will strike you down.

20:17.092 --> 20:18.717
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

20:18.718 --> 20:20.886
What were your audition
experiences like?

20:20.887 --> 20:23.972
- Mine was sort of
the chemistry read.

20:23.973 --> 20:26.809
So I go through the audition
and put everything out,

20:26.810 --> 20:29.103
and I'm there for three hours.

20:29.104 --> 20:34.234
And by the end of the audition,
I start running a 103 fever...

20:34.359 --> 20:36.193
- Oh, gosh.
- And go home.

20:36.194 --> 20:37.904
And I'm in bed
for, like, four days.

20:38.029 --> 20:40.072
So at the time,
I have left the audition.

20:40.073 --> 20:43.909
I'm like,
there's actually nothing left.

20:43.910 --> 20:47.788
So I think whatever I had left
was in that room.

20:47.789 --> 20:51.334
- I remember I'd sent a tape.
Crazy tape.

20:51.459 --> 20:53.502
