coming with me?

36:02.620 --> 36:04.497
I'd like to teach you
how to toss your hair.

36:07.167 --> 36:08.835
Ready?

36:09.002 --> 36:10.836
Now, this is
a slightly different technique

36:10.837 --> 36:12.881
because I have a ponytail
today.

36:13.006 --> 36:15.049
But I have to wind it up.

36:15.050 --> 36:18.011
And then you toss, toss.

36:20.055 --> 36:21.389
[gasps]

36:21.514 --> 36:24.392
[cheers and applause]

36:28.480 --> 36:31.231
No notes, Rem.

36:31.232 --> 36:32.691
It's been a pleasure.

36:32.692 --> 36:35.944
I have one more thing
before you go,

36:35.945 --> 36:37.572
a parting gift.

36:42.577 --> 36:44.119
This is my training wand.

36:44.120 --> 36:45.871
I hope you enjoy it.

36:45.872 --> 36:48.123
Thank you, Remy.
Can I have a hug?

36:48.124 --> 36:51.169
[cheers and applause]

36:54.255 --> 36:55.506
You're amazing.

36:55.507 --> 36:56.883
Thank you so much.

36:57.008 --> 36:58.425
Everyone, Remington.

36:58.426 --> 37:01.388
[cheers and applause]

37:11.189 --> 37:12.815
Well, hello.

37:12.816 --> 37:15.860
[cheers and applause]

37:19.364 --> 37:20.573
[bell dings]

37:20.699 --> 37:24.452
♪ And though you protest ♪

37:24.577 --> 37:28.456
♪ Your disinterest ♪

37:28.581 --> 37:35.379
♪ I know clandestinely ♪

37:35.380 --> 37:37.465
♪ You're gonna
grin and bear it ♪

37:37.590 --> 37:39.675
♪ Your newfound popularity ♪

37:39.676 --> 37:41.261
[squeals]

37:41.386 --> 37:46.433
♪ La, la, la, la ♪

37:46.558 --> 37:51.604
♪ La, la, la, la ♪

37:51.730 --> 37:53.814
♪ La, la ♪

37:53.815 --> 37:59.236
♪ Ooh ♪

37:59.237 --> 38:03.282
♪ You'll be popular ♪

38:03.283 --> 38:06.660
♪ Just not quite as popular ♪

38:06.661 --> 38:12.500
♪ As me ♪

38:12.625 --> 38:15.503
[cheers and applause]

38:20.467 --> 38:27.349
♪ ♪

38:40.945 --> 38:43.614
<i>- After the break,
a breathtaking performance</i>

38:43.615 --> 38:46.451
<i>from the Gershwin Theatre
when Ariana and Cynthia</i>

38:46.576 --> 38:49.662
<i>join Stephen Schwartz
and two very special guests.</i>

38:54.000 --> 38:55.377
["One Short Day" playing]

38:56.586 --> 39:00.756
- Please welcome Ethan Slater
and Bowen Yang.

39:00.757 --> 39:07.847
♪ ♪

39:12.185 --> 39:13.560
- Hello.
- Grab me now.

39:13.561 --> 39:15.313
- We're here, Bowen.
You got this.

39:15.438 --> 39:17.899
- Please excuse our appearance.
- Sorry.

39:18.024 --> 39:22.528
- We were watching Ariana
and Remy perform "Popular"

39:22.529 --> 39:24.988
backstage and got
a little overexcited

39:24.989 --> 39:26.282
during the hair toss.

39:26.408 --> 39:27.741
- Yeah.

39:27.742 --> 39:30.285
So to all the kids
watching at home,

39:30.286 --> 39:34.915
remember to stretch
before you toss.

39:34.916 --> 39:38.544
Now, back to what
really matters.

39:38.545 --> 39:40.714
<i>We go now to the iconic
Gershwin Theatre</i>

39:40.839 --> 39:42.549
<i>in New York City,
the original home</i>

39:42.674 --> 39:44.508
<i>of the Broadway production
"Wicked."</i>

39:44.509 --> 39:47.470
<i>Accompanied by the
incomparable Stephen Schwartz,</i>

39:47.595 --> 39:49.431
<i>with a special arrangement
and performance</i>

39:49.556 --> 39:53.518
<i>just for tonight,
this is "For Good."</i>

39:53.643 --> 39:56.438
[soft piano music]

39:56.563 --> 40:03.528
♪ ♪

40:09.701 --> 40:10.994
- Hey, guys.

40:11.119 --> 40:13.329
- Hi.
- We're at the Gershwin.

40:13.455 --> 40:14.455
- I know.

40:14.456 --> 40:16.331
- Who thought
that would happen?

40:16.332 --> 40:18.126
- I don't know.
- You guys look beautiful.

40:18.251 --> 40:19.585
You should probably
sing something.

40:19.586 --> 40:20.919
What do you think?
- I think it's a good idea.

40:20.920 --> 40:22.004
- All right.
Let's do it.

40:22.005 --> 40:23.672
- Why not?
- How about this?

40:23.673 --> 40:26.550
["For Good" playing]

40:26.551 --> 40:33.641
♪ ♪

40:36.978 --> 40:40.397
- ♪ I've heard it said ♪

40:40.398 --> 40:44.068
♪ That people come
into our lives ♪

40:44.069 --> 40:47.072
♪ For a reason ♪

40:47.197 --> 40:50.742
♪ Bringing something
we must learn ♪

40:50.867 --> 40:53.787
♪ And we are led ♪

40:53.912 --> 40:57.831
♪ To those
who help us most to grow ♪

40:57.832 --> 41:01.585
♪ If we let them ♪

41:01.586 --> 41:04.213
♪ And we help them in return ♪

41:04.214 --> 41:06.215
♪ ♪

41:06.216 --> 41:12.096
♪ Well, I don't know
if I believe that's true ♪

41:12.097 --> 41:15.599
♪ But I know
I'm who I am today ♪

41:15.600 --> 41:20.771
♪ Because I knew you ♪

41:20.772 --> 41:24.400
♪ Like a comet
pulled from orbit ♪

41:24.401 --> 41:27.654
♪ As it passes a sun ♪

41:27.779 --> 41:31.740
♪ Like a stream
that meets a boulder ♪

41:31.741 --> 41:35.412
♪ Halfway through the wood ♪

41:35.537 --> 41:41.668
♪ Who can say if I've been
changed for the better? ♪

41:41.793 --> 41:45.754
♪ But because I knew you ♪

41:45.755 --> 41:49.049
♪ ♪

41:49.050 --> 41:53.929
♪ I have been changed ♪

41:53.930 --> 41:56.558
♪ For good ♪

41:56.683 --> 42:00.269
♪ ♪

42:00.270 --> 42:03.647
- ♪ It well may be ♪

42:03.648 --> 42:06.900
♪ That we will
never meet again ♪

42:06.901 --> 42:09.737
♪ In this lifetime ♪

42:09.738 --> 42:13.491
♪ So let me say
before we part ♪

42:13.616 --> 42:17.454
♪ So much of me is made ♪

42:17.579 --> 42:20.122
♪ Of what I learned from you ♪

42:20.123 --> 42:23.585
♪ You'll be with me ♪

42:23.710 --> 42:27.714
♪ Like a handprint
on my heart ♪

42:27.839 --> 42:33.427
♪ And now
whatever way our stories end ♪

42:33.428 --> 42:36.472
♪ I know
you have rewritten mine ♪

42:36.473 --> 42:41.101
♪ By being my friend ♪

42:41.102 --> 42:44.229
♪ Like a ship blown
from its mooring ♪

42:44.230 --> 42:47.525
♪ By a wind off the sea ♪

42:47.650 --> 42:51.153
♪ Like a seed dropped
by a skybird ♪

42:51.154 --> 42:54.865
♪ In a distant wood ♪

42:54.866 --> 43:00.580
♪ Who can say if I've been
changed for the better ♪

43:00.705 --> 43:04.501
♪ But because I knew you ♪

43:04.626 --> 43:07.753
- ♪ Because I knew you ♪

43:07.754 --> 43:13.343
both: * I have been
changed for good ♪

43:13.468 --> 43:16.262
- ♪ The years go by so fast ♪

43:16.388 --> 43:18.473
♪ The flames keep burning ♪

43:18.598 --> 43:23.894
♪ But we know someday
it could be gone ♪

43:23.895 --> 43:26.272
- ♪ It's nice to know then ♪

43:26.398 --> 43:29.693
♪ As the torch gets passed ♪

43:29.818 --> 43:35.657
both: * You will keep it
blazing brightly on ♪

43:35.782 --> 43:37.408
both: * Like a comet
pulled from orbit ♪

43:37.409 --> 43:39.576
both: * Like a ship blown
from its mooring ♪

43:39.577 --> 43:41.078
both: * As it passes the sun ♪

43:41.079 --> 43:42.788
both: * By a wind off the sea ♪

43:42.789 --> 43:44.374
both: * Like a stream
that meets a boulder ♪

43:44.499 --> 43:46.458
both: * Like a seed dropped
by a bird in the wood ♪

43:46.459 --> 43:49.753
both:
♪ Halfway through the wood ♪

43:49.754 --> 43:53.465
both: * Who can say ♪

43:53.466 --> 43:59.304
♪ If I've been changed
for the better ♪

43:59.305 --> 44:02.809
both: * I do believe
I have been ♪

44:02.934 --> 44:07.938
♪ Changed for the better ♪

44:07.939 --> 44:12.986
- ♪ And because I knew you ♪
- ♪ Because I knew you ♪

44:13.111 --> 44:18.574
- ♪ Because I knew you ♪
- ♪ Because I knew you ♪

44:18.575 --> 44:23.829
all: * Because I knew you ♪

44:23.830 --> 44:30.545
♪ I have been changed ♪

44:30.670 --> 44:34.089
♪ ♪

44:34.090 --> 44:39.763
♪ For good ♪

44:54.903 --> 44:56.029
- There's such a capacity
for the fans

44:57.072 --> 45:00.282
to love the films
alongside the musical,

45:00.283 --> 45:01.493
alongside the books,

45:01.618 --> 45:03.160
alongside
the L. Frank Baum books.

45:03.161 --> 45:05.204
Like, it is more likely
than not

45:05.205 --> 45:08.040
that fans are
a little bit adversarial

45:08.041 --> 45:10.418
towards the newer thing,
the newer installment,

45:10.585 --> 45:12.378
the newer imagination
of something.

45:12.379 --> 45:13.921
I think the fact
that none of us

45:13.922 --> 45:17.091
have really encountered any
sort of like, I don't know--

45:17.092 --> 45:19.135
- Pushback.
- Pushback is so meaningful.

45:19.260 --> 45:21.804
- We're very lucky to have been
embraced by the fans

45:21.805 --> 45:23.514
the way we have.

45:23.515 --> 45:25.683
The "Wicked" fans are the most
beautiful souls in the world.

45:25.684 --> 45:27.310
And they're fiercely loving.
- Yeah.

45:27.435 --> 45:29.979
- Oh, my gosh.
- They're so insanely loving.

45:30.146 --> 45:31.772
It's crazy.

45:31.773 --> 45:33.691
- The love and passion
that you've poured

45:33.692 --> 45:37.946
into each character
has really allowed them

45:38.113 --> 45:42.199
and opened their hearts
and minds to us.

45:42.200 --> 45:43.742
- We all love our characters.

45:43.743 --> 45:46.662
I remember you defending
the Wizard to the end.

45:46.663 --> 45:49.332
And, you know, I don't know
if that's how you feel

45:49.499 --> 45:51.710
now that we're out of it,
but you have to, like, love--

45:51.835 --> 45:53.211
you have to love
your character.

45:53.336 --> 45:54.379
And so I love Boq so much.

45:54.504 --> 45:55.546
- I was there too. Yeah.
- Yeah.

45:55.547 --> 45:58.298
- I take away a lot
from you guys.

45:58.299 --> 46:01.969
But what helps me is, like,
when I look into your eyes,

46:01.970 --> 46:05.806
and I see Elphaba, and I see
all the complexities there.

46:05.807 --> 46:07.891
Then you find that exchange.

46:07.892 --> 46:11.311
And I love when I look at you,
you're, like, fresh and naive.

46:11.312 --> 46:13.106
And then Jon will
come up to me and say,

46:13.231 --> 46:15.315
scare the hell out of Ariana.

46:15.316 --> 46:16.484
And I'm like, are you sure?

46:16.609 --> 46:18.028
He says, yes.

46:18.153 --> 46:20.988
So I just turned and ran
at her, literally like--

46:20.989 --> 46:23.158
[shouting]

46:23.324 --> 46:25.075
This poor--
- Best moment of my life.

46:25.076 --> 46:28.746
- She dropped onto the couch.

46:28.747 --> 46:30.914
- [gasps]

46:30.915 --> 46:32.334
- Wave.

46:34.586 --> 46:37.129
And shut your mouth!

46:37.130 --> 46:41.176
- She was so scared,
a contact lens popped out.

46:41.301 --> 46:42.635
[laughs]

46:42.761 --> 46:47.182
- [laughing]
My contact came out.

46:47.307 --> 46:50.643
I'm sorry, y'all.
My contact came out.

46:50.769 --> 46:52.145
- It was
a really cherished moment.

46:52.270 --> 46:54.064
- I loved scaring you.
[laughter]

46:54.189 --> 46:55.732
- I savor every minute.

46:55.899 --> 46:57.525
- And now you--let's get
to this half of the room,

46:57.650 --> 46:59.401
because I want to hear
about this.

46:59.402 --> 47:01.528
- Bowen, what about Pfannee?
- Bowen. The besties.

47:01.529 --> 47:06.283
- I've learned, like,
the danger of cruelty from him.

47:06.284 --> 47:08.410
These are two people
who are, like, bullies.

47:08.411 --> 47:10.412
And they--and they--
and they execute and motivate

47:10.413 --> 47:13.375
other people to do bad things.

47:13.541 --> 47:15.460
But I would apologize
to Cynthia between takes

47:15.585 --> 47:19.547
and be like, that felt awful,
like, being cruel to you.

47:19.714 --> 47:22.257
So I think--I don't know,
I think as you age,

47:22.258 --> 47:24.344
you just soften a little bit
in those ways, hopefully.

47:24.469 --> 47:25.803
And I feel like
that is the thing

47:25.804 --> 47:27.179
that I've taken away from him.

47:27.180 --> 47:29.265
- Yes. Yeah. Yeah.

47:29.391 --> 47:31.350
- We're so privileged
to have been able to be there,

47:31.351 --> 47:33.018
to witness each other's moments

47:33.019 --> 47:35.146
and see every single take
of everything

47:35.271 --> 47:37.399
because the movie
is so beautiful.

47:37.565 --> 47:38.900
And everyone is
so brilliant in it.

47:39.025 --> 47:40.734
But it was so special
to be there

47:40.735 --> 47:44.114
and see everyone's process
and every single ad lib

47:44.239 --> 47:45.989
and every single choice
that everyone made.

47:45.990 --> 47:48.158
And it was just such a treat.

47:48.159 --> 47:51.620
- Well done, everyone.
- Yeah.

47:51.621 --> 47:55.666
<i>- Please welcome Bowen Yang
and Ariana Grande.</i>

47:55.667 --> 47:59.254
["One Short Day" playing]

47:59.379 --> 48:01.380
- You know,
when you think about it,

48:01.381 --> 48:04.842
"Wicked" is a film at its core
about friendship.

48:04.843 --> 48:06.553
- I couldn't agree more.
- Yes.

48:06.678 --> 48:07.886
Friendship between two people

48:07.887 --> 48:09.889
who couldn't be more different
from each other.

48:10.015 --> 48:12.558
- Yes, a popular,
ambitious sorcery student

48:12.559 --> 48:14.977
with impeccable style
and a love for all things pink.

48:14.978 --> 48:16.937
- And her best friend Pfannee.

48:16.938 --> 48:20.441
[laughter]

48:20.442 --> 48:22.860
- Oh.

48:22.861 --> 48:24.779
- What?

48:24.946 --> 48:26.156
- No, nothing.
I just thought you were--

48:26.322 --> 48:28.949
I thought you were going
to say, you know, Elphaba.

48:28.950 --> 48:30.367
- Elphaba?

48:30.368 --> 48:32.619
Really?

48:32.620 --> 48:34.496
- Well, yeah.

48:34.497 --> 48:36.332
- Oh, well--

48:36.458 --> 48:38.542
- That's, like, the core
friendship of the whole movie.

48:38.543 --> 48:40.837
- I don't know.

48:40.962 --> 48:43.839
I feel like "Wicked" is a story
about a popular girl

48:43.840 --> 48:47.635
and an equally popular guy
who loves to follow her around,

48:47.802 --> 48:49.345
carry her books,
and occasionally makes

48:49.346 --> 48:51.139
catty little comments
about their ugly classmates.

48:51.264 --> 48:52.181
- I really don't think
that's what

48:52.182 --> 48:53.724
people are taking away from--

48:53.725 --> 48:55.267
but yeah.

48:55.268 --> 48:58.313
- Well, art is subjective.

48:58.438 --> 48:59.646
- Yeah, it is.

48:59.647 --> 49:00.856
That's true.

49:00.857 --> 49:02.358
I love you.
- I love you.

49:02.359 --> 49:05.861
- So much.
- So much.

49:05.862 --> 49:09.865
- In the meantime,
performing "I'm Not That Girl,"

49:09.866 --> 49:14.370
please welcome the phenomenal,
the singular Cynthia Erivo.

49:14.371 --> 49:18.958
[cheers and applause]

49:19.084 --> 49:21.877
["I'm Not That Girl" playing]

49:21.878 --> 49:24.839
[yearning music]

49:24.964 --> 49:31.930
♪ ♪

49:42.565 --> 49:45.901
- ♪ Hands touch ♪

49:45.902 --> 49:49.697
♪ Eyes meet ♪

49:49.698 --> 49:52.742
♪ Sudden silence ♪

49:52.909 --> 49:56.704
♪ Sudden heat ♪

49:56.705 --> 49:58.914
♪ Hearts leap ♪

49:58.915 --> 50:03.460
♪ In a giddy whirl ♪

50:03.461 --> 50:09.801
♪ He could be that boy ♪

50:09.926 --> 50:16.141
♪ But I'm not that girl ♪

50:16.266 --> 50:19.768
♪ Don't dream ♪

50:19.769 --> 50:23.313
♪ Too far ♪

50:23.314 --> 50:29.820
♪ Don't lose sight
of who you are ♪

50:29.821 --> 50:36.785
♪ Don't remember
that rush of joy ♪

50:36.786 --> 50:43.125
♪ He could be that boy ♪

50:43.126 --> 50:48.505
♪ I'm not that girl ♪

50:48.506 --> 50:53.761
♪ Every so often,
we long to steal ♪

50:53.762 --> 50:58.182
♪ To the land
of what-might-have-been ♪

50:58.183 --> 51:03.395
♪ But that doesn't soften
the ache we feel ♪

51:03.396 --> 51:09.610
♪ When reality sets back in ♪

51:09.611 --> 51:13.822
♪ ♪

51:13.823 --> 51:17.326
♪ Blithe smile ♪

51:17.327 --> 51:20.704
♪ Lithe limb ♪

51:20.705 --> 51:23.333
♪ She who's winsome ♪

51:23.458 --> 51:27.337
♪ She wins him ♪

51:27.462 --> 51:29.713
♪ Gold hair ♪

51:29.714 --> 51:34.094
♪ With a gentle curl ♪

51:34.260 --> 51:40.683
♪ That's the girl he chose ♪

51:40.684 --> 51:47.356
♪ And heaven knows ♪

51:47.357 --> 51:53.195
♪ I'm not that girl ♪

51:53.196 --> 51:56.156
[vocalizing]

51:56.157 --> 52:02.330
♪ ♪

52:03.832 --> 52:06.333
♪ Don't wish ♪

52:06.334 --> 52:10.212
♪ Don't start ♪

52:10.213 --> 52:16.176
♪ Wishing only wounds
the heart ♪

52:16.177 --> 52:19.013
♪ I wasn't born ♪

52:19.014 --> 52:25.020
♪ For the rose and pearl ♪

52:25.145 --> 52:26.937
♪ ♪

52:26.938 --> 52:33.944
♪ There's a girl I know ♪

52:33.945 --> 52:39.450
♪ He loves her so ♪

52:39.451 --> 52:43.245
♪ Mm ♪

52:43.246 --> 52:50.085
♪ I'm not that girl ♪

52:50.086 --> 52:57.177
♪ ♪

53:00.347 --> 53:04.142
[cheers and applause]

53:04.309 --> 53:06.394
Thank you.
[laughs]

53:10.023 --> 53:17.030
♪ ♪

53:26.164 --> 53:28.500
["One Short Day" playing]

53:29.834 --> 53:33.003
<i>- And now, please welcome
the director of "Wicked"</i>

53:33.004 --> 53:36.298
<i>and "Wicked: For Good"
Jon M. Chu.</i>

53:36.299 --> 53:39.260
[cheers and applause]

53:39.386 --> 53:45.224
♪ ♪

53:45.225 --> 53:47.101
- Wow.

53:47.102 --> 53:48.228
I am Jon M. Chu.

53:48.353 --> 53:50.438
I am the director of "Wicked."

53:53.066 --> 53:56.485
Four-plus years of my life
poured into this.

53:56.486 --> 54:00.239
My wife had three kids
during this.

54:00.240 --> 54:01.573
Superstar.

54:01.574 --> 54:03.952
Anyway,
directing this movie has been

54:04.077 --> 54:05.745
one of the highlights
of my career,

54:05.870 --> 54:07.496
but I knew
from the very beginning,

54:07.497 --> 54:10.040
I had to get the casting
just right.

54:10.041 --> 54:12.042
And we ended up
with the perfect cast.

54:12.043 --> 54:16.255
Right?
[cheers and applause]

54:16.256 --> 54:18.341
But I have to tell you all

54:18.466 --> 54:21.261
that so many different people
wanted to be in "Wicked"

54:21.386 --> 54:23.012
and sent us
their casting tapes.

54:23.013 --> 54:24.013
You may have heard this.

54:24.014 --> 54:25.639
And tonight,
for the first time,

54:25.640 --> 54:27.934
we are sharing
some of the unseen footage

54:28.059 --> 54:30.811
from the "Wicked" auditions.

54:30.812 --> 54:32.647
Take a look.

54:34.065 --> 54:37.318
<i>["Defying Gravity" playing]</i>

54:37.444 --> 54:38.862
- My name is
Chris "Ludacris" Bridges,

54:38.987 --> 54:42.114
and I'll be reading for Glinda
because I want to show people

54:42.115 --> 54:43.741
that I have range.

54:43.742 --> 54:45.534
- Lainey Wilson
reading for Elphaba.

54:45.535 --> 54:46.952
- My name is Ben Schwartz.

54:46.953 --> 54:49.664
- I'm Rob Gronkowski,
a.k.a. The Gronk.

54:49.789 --> 54:51.665
- Do me a favor.
Don't stand there. Thank you.

54:51.666 --> 54:53.167
- Hi, I'm Shaquille O'Neal,

54:53.168 --> 54:56.587
and I'm reading for the part
of Munchkin Number Five.

54:56.588 --> 54:59.382
- Seven.
- Oh, Munchkin Number Seven.

54:59.507 --> 55:02.134
- I'm Khloe Kardashian,
and I'm auditioning for Glinda

55:02.135 --> 55:03.510
because she's a good bitch.

55:03.511 --> 55:05.804
I mean, witch. Witch.

55:05.805 --> 55:08.766
- ♪ So if you care to find me ♪

55:08.767 --> 55:11.560
- ♪ Look to the western sky ♪

55:11.561 --> 55:14.438
- ♪ Ew, I'll show you
what shoes to wear ♪

55:14.439 --> 55:17.024
- I am auditioning
for the part of Glinda.

55:17.025 --> 55:19.401
Toss, toss.

55:19.402 --> 55:21.111
Hello.

55:21.112 --> 55:24.490
- ♪ The toughest case
I've yet to face ♪

55:24.491 --> 55:25.950
♪ Don't worry ♪

55:26.076 --> 55:27.327
♪ I'm determined ♪

55:27.452 --> 55:31.331
- ♪ You could be that boy ♪

55:31.456 --> 55:34.249
♪ And I could be that girl ♪

55:34.250 --> 55:35.834
- Five, six, seven, eight.

55:35.835 --> 55:38.295
♪ And if I'm flying solo ♪

55:38.296 --> 55:40.382
♪ At least I'm-- ♪
What's that?

55:40.507 --> 55:42.383
She's already been cast?
Not a problem.

55:42.384 --> 55:43.801
Not a problem.

55:43.802 --> 55:44.886
I didn't know
which character, so--

55:45.011 --> 55:46.428
♪ Popular ♪

55:46.429 --> 55:48.431
- ♪ You're gonna be popular ♪

55:48.556 --> 55:50.182
- ♪ Popular ♪

55:50.183 --> 55:51.392
- Popular.

55:51.393 --> 55:53.185
You gon' be popular.

55:53.186 --> 55:54.646
- ♪ I'll teach you
the proper ploys ♪

55:54.771 --> 55:56.022
♪ When you talk to boys ♪

55:56.147 --> 55:57.398
- ♪ You're gonna be pop-- ♪

55:57.399 --> 55:58.565
What's that?

55:58.566 --> 56:00.068
She's cast as well?

56:00.193 --> 56:01.485
So who do you want me
to audition--

56:01.486 --> 56:02.778
flying monkey.

56:02.779 --> 56:03.862
Sure.

56:03.863 --> 56:04.947
Yeah, you got it.

56:04.948 --> 56:05.907
♪ I'm just a fly-- ♪

56:06.032 --> 56:07.074
He doesn't sing?

56:07.075 --> 56:08.909
Or talk? OK.

56:08.910 --> 56:11.995
- ♪ I wanna be on the broom
